absorption traffic jam in your gut our  body is  well equipped to send out the right  cocktail of enzymes to help your body  break down whatever is on board also if  we want to get really nitpicky  having some fat in there may actually  improve the absorption of nutrients in  something like celery juice since its  vitamin a and k  are fat soluble and are therefore better  absorbed with a little bit of fat  also i know i've discussed this in  previous videos but there are no  benefits of celery juice beyond just  getting in some extra fluids and a few  micronutrients  it's not detoxing it doesn't inherently  clear up your skin improve mood or boost  energy and if it does lead to weight  loss it's because it's only got like 40  calories per cup celery is also rich in  fodmaps which when consumed in excess  can cause  well  the runs  [Music]  what are you doing it's coming out of me  like lava so  yeah  i guess if diarrhea is caroline's  definition of a good morning detox or if  it's her top weight loss hack then  yeah i guess this makes some sense  it's also worth flagging that caroline  breaks her own rule with the celery  juice which she suggests she drinks as  early as 10 a.m news flash folks celery  juice like all foods or drinks with  calories will break a fast and yes i  realize that that's almost a moot point  because as i said before  the main benefits of fasting for weight  loss is not the reduction in insulin  release but rather just basically  reduced calorie consumption and like i  said celery juice is very very low in  calories so many big holes in these  suggestions i don't know how this boat  is not gonna sink  anyway  aside from all the low calorie fluids  the first meal of caroline's day is the  post workout green smoothie so her  smoothie recipes change slightly day to  day but they generally follow the same  format of having mostly greens some  fruit and water so day one for example  is a handful of celery stalks one bunch  of parsley two large swiss chard leaves  a frozen banana a handful of frozen or  fresh pineapple and one cup of water  sounds  um  nutrition  now while i appreciate the solid variety  of fruit and veggies in here  i would love to see some fats in protein  to really bump up the satiety factor and  like i said improve the absorption of  those fat soluble vitamins so maybe some  nut butter protein powder silken tofu or  a higher protein plant-based milk like  pea or soy which i know yes i know these  are suggestions that defy her bs rules  interestingly  caroline actually explicitly says that  her smoothie isn't intended for it to  keep her full  she actually wants to digest it quickly  so then she can just get on with her  lunch i mean i've never understood this  concept like if weight loss is your goal  why would it seem like a good idea to  drink almost 200 calories that will not  even contribute to satiety  anyways i digress moving on lunch  usually consists of the infamous mono  meal  aka just a ton of fruit so on day one  for example she recommends 13 pounds of  watermelon 13 freaking pounds  that is probably not gonna feel so good  at least it wouldn't for me  watermelon is considered high fodmap and  consuming it in excess can cause a lot  of bloating diarrhea and other digestive  issues in folks with sensitive guts so  yeah i wouldn't be  loving that meal now on day eight  caroline switches it up a bit and  suggests that you can have a large plate  of watermelon followed by 20 figs or 10  dates because apparently  this order of consumption helps to  reduce the bloat again it's now quite  clear to me that we can add food  combining to the list of pseudoscience  wellness gimmicks that caroline  subscribes to again there is no evidence  that eating food in a particular order  will improve digestion or reduce  bloating like your body doesn't know or  care if you eat your watermelon or your  figs first but you know what actually  helps to reduce bloating um  not eating huge amounts of high fodmap  fruit anyways caroline claims that the  reason she likes watermelon is because  of its alkalinizing properties so yeah  we're really going through that wellness  culture bs bingo card today  folks  foods cannot i repeat  cannot change the ph of your blood and  therefore their acidic or alkaline  characteristics mean nothing at all our  body actually has a very sophisticated  buffer system to manage variations in  the ph of foods and if it didn't  she wouldn't be doing so well after her  one and a half liters of lemon water  this is not going so great moving on to  dinner we are largely looking at salads  or salad ingredients wrapped in like a  sheet of nori under the faulty pretense  of being a rat all of these dinners also  contain some kind of oil-free salad  dressing made up of pureed vegetables  herbs seeds and vinegar she also  sometimes incorporates a side of  potatoes or sweet potatoes with her  dinner but says that you should eat your  salad first and then the potatoes for  optimal digestion again there's no  scientific reason for this it is not  surprisingly just more of that food  combining bs now when i checked out  caroline's instagram for her personal  wedding days i found them to be pretty  much exactly what is presented here  lemon water celery juice a crap ton of  fruit salad and potatoes so carbs on  carbs on carbs with a load of water and  a crap ton of fiber so  at least she practices what she preaches  anyway this all sounds like total  torture to me and i probably wouldn't be  able to leave the house on a plane like  this out of fear of  my pants but if you were feeling ballsy  or just like really lonely and you  wanted to go out for dinner  your options would be  pretty sad for instance when eating at  an italian restaurant caroline suggests  ordering a plain green salad with mashed  avocado as the dressing and then having  plain tomato pasta with no cheese  sounds like a great time to meet but if  you do the safe thing and eat all of  your meals at home you might actually  need an industrial sized kitchen  just to accommodate your next walmart  haul caroline's menu includes over 30  large bulky produce items that require  refrigeration including 15 heads of  celery and 14 heads of lettuce  and this is for just one person  if your partner or kids want to eat  something other than like canned tuna  out of the pantry  i'm sorry but  they are apparently  out of luck the shopping list also  includes 25 lemons two watermelons two  honey melons and six honeydew melons  ringing in at about 500  for the 10 days considering how  unsatisfied you're likely to feel on  this diet that is actually insane  and on that note let's take a look at  the stats so when i analyzed a few of  the 10 days on the weight loss stream i  found that on average you're looking at  around 2 500 calories but sometimes as  many as 4 000 calories with up to 82  percent of calories from carbs and the  rest from protein and fat  so on a lot of those days we're looking  at a pretty skewed macronutrient split  basically the plan is veg and fruit  heavy and rich in fiber water and volume  which generally may help folks looking  to lose weight but ultimately it does  come down to calories and i would bet  that most women who struggle with their  weight  wouldn't lose a lot of weight if they  ate four thousand calories of straight  up carbs there's also an exorbitant  amount of fiber here  now considering that most north  americans don't even meet the 25 to 37  gram recommendation  consuming four to five times that amount  in high fodmap foods  is surely going to wreak havoc on most  people's guts now honestly there is so  much wrong here i don't even know where  to start with the recommendations  but i think we just gotta like  start fresh no mono meals no to food  combining  no to celery juice and alkaline diets no  no no  for a diet averaging 2500 calories which  is a normal healthy amount of calories  to consume for a lot of people we need  to see more protein and fat to help  promote satiety without the digestive  stress and without needing to be eating  like all day long my jaw is hurting just  thinking about chewing all of that fruit  now i just want to close with a brief  discussion on some of the major  problematic themes here because if you  didn't have a shaky relationship with  food before you bought this reset plan  you absolutely will after first of all  the fact that caroline claims that this  diet isn't restrictive is an actual  trolling joke you're restricted from  animal-based products refined sugar oil  and gluten  and you're limited to very small amounts  of whole grains beans legumes soy and  even whole foods sources of fat like  nuts and seeds  you're also restricted to when you can  eat via intermittent fasting and also  the order that you're supposed to eat  foods in like could you make eating any  more complicated if someone were to lose  weight on a diet like this it would  probably be because they were so  stressed and overwhelmed with all of the  rules they might just say  it's too much of a hassle to even have a  meal now i also looked at a bunch of  caroline's instagram posts and found  them to be riddled with diet culture and  pseudoscience  from demonizing sugar to suggesting  monomials to deep bloat to sharing  recipes for a flat tummy etc  this account is toxic hard stop  so in conclusion caroline's ebook is so  confusing and misinformed i am not even  sure how it makes sense in her head if  you do this for 10 days you will likely  be very hungry unsatisfied and actually  probably very bloated and if you do this  for longer you will be likely  malnourished if you lose weight it will  be from water or from sheer unhappiness  and boredom from all of the mono meals  and crazy rules and if you don't lose  weight it's because you're eating  massive portions of fruit in either  scenario your relationship with food is  sure to suffer so i just really don't  see what the possible benefit could be  i'm sorry but there are better ways to  spend your hard-earned cash than this  body reset so for so many reasons i give  this a huge pass and on that note that  is all that i have for you guys today if  you like this video be sure to give it  the thumbs up leave me a comment below  on who you'd like to see me review next  subscribe to the channel and i will see  you next time on abby's kitchen bye  and for more great videos like this  check out the link right here  you
 

